[Music]  here at the final four there is probably  one thing that every fan whether a  jayhawk wildcat blue devil or tar heel  can agree upon a trip to new orleans is  not complete without a stop at cafe  dumont french for cafe of the world it  has become just that known globally for  its coffee and beignets which are square  french style donuts served in powdered  sugar still housed in the heart of the  french quarter where it was established  in 1862  cafe du monde has also been a family  affair since the 1940s when the  fernandez family purchased the  restaurant i caught up with jay roman  part of the family's third generation  now savoring the flavor their family  helps bring to new orleans  [Music]  it's the new orleans party  open to all  cafe dumont  it's green and white awning on decatur  street as famous as its lines this lady  would like an order of beignets can you  take care of her for me  [Applause]  thank you which are always worth the  wait come on down here i don't think  this menu is going to make it to the top  that's all right that's why they give  you three you have two more to go when  we get there  two more pieces of pastry and powdered  sugar perfection cafe dumont's signature  beignets do you know how many calories  are in one  i don't think we don't count calories in  new orleans that's who you know we are a  food city and and calories don't count  we check them at the board i like that  true or not the beignets are a french  quarter staple made and served fresh  the recipe basics roll dough cut into  squares tossed into the fryer by hand  then coated in the white stuff is there  a way to make the perfect beignet the  biggest thing is is when you roll it out  and then put it in the oil you want to  make sure the oil is hot enough because  that's what's going to get it to puff up  and the  secret to keeping the powdered sugar at  least until i dump it all over myself  basically on the beignet is just when  they're hot when they're hot you put it  on and if you can sift it you know to do  something to get it on a smooth coat and  then when you're biting the beignet is  don't breathe in or breathe out it's  just kind of hold your breath and go for  it  yep there goes the sugar  how do you not love that  oh my god i know i look ridiculous right  now not at all we like that look  after a few more bites kind of use your  fingers a little bit to separate them i  tried my hands at making some and trying  to keep the shape and found it's not as  easy as it looks put it in but don't put  it in with too much force oil is very  hot  close and then we just just give it a  little push  so afraid of that i mean that's good  that's what i want everybody afraid of  that oil i missed my first free throw i  can do it that's okay you'll do better  yeah you did i think i was a little  afraid all right so this oh my gosh very  close or the third but now i understand  why they're all there you go perfect  you'll get everything you need jay roman  has been surrounded by beignets his  entire life his grandfather hubert  fernandez bought cafe dumond in 1942  it's been their family legacy ever since  i have a 15 month old granddaughter who  is getting ready to eat her first  beignet her mom is you know  making her grow a couple more teeth  before she lets her gather but she will  be taking her first bite of a beignet  shortly i'm thinking about you as a  young kid running around with powdered  sugar all over you this had to be a  dream come true it was perfect we  enjoyed you know it was okay until you  get to the old enough and then they made  you sweep the floor but even working had  its benefits my daughter graduated from  tulane just a few years ago in an  industry known for keeping those in it  away from family at cafe du monde they  continue to be surrounded by it i got to  go to work with dad or i got to go work  with my uncles you know that was  something i looked forward to doing so i  always tried when my kids were growing  up to not tell them this is what they  were going to do you know let them see  for themselves it is something they  wanted and now now they do i have two  children both of them are working in the  business and doing well with it the  family isn't the only thing intertwined  with cafe du monde so is new orleans  itself people talk about new orleans as  the gumbo pot you know a mixture of a  whole lot of things and we're just very  proud to be one of the one of the  ingredients in that pipe with a history  that dates back to 1862  it's no wonder that's when cafe dumont  began as a coffee stand in what's now  the french market the chicory coffee it  served the same you get today chicory is  the root of the endive which is a  lettuce and that is roasted and ground  and mixed with the coffee the original  settlers to new orleans had very short  supplies the trick they used to stretch  their supplies was to add  the endive to the coffee it developed  its own taste in the taste duck why did  your grandfather decide that he had to  buy cafe dumont you know he just sat  across the street and again you got to  remember 1942 this wasn't uh it wasn't a  lot of tourism in new orleans in 1942  but he just had a vision from coffee  stand to cafe to 10 locations around new  orleans there's even merchandise and  shipping nationwide but when in the  crescent city the original decatur  street location is the must-visit spot  not only for tourists one of the times  bill clinton was here in new orleans and  he was getting ready to leave driving my  kids to school and they were on the  radio saying he's late you know but he  must be going for beignets at cafe de  mon with that my cell phone rang and it  was my guy downtown saying the secret  service is here even with the celebrity  status and the growth cafe du monde  remains true to its roots we have one  food product you the beignets that's it  it's really good  we hope so but i mean it is it is our  only food product the cafe is with milk  the beverages for for a number of years  when i was growing up we had coffee and  we had cold milk and over the years  we've expanded a little bit people have  developed taste for iced coffee and  frozen coffee and  but still is a very simple menu is it  tempting in what this world has become  in food to get the gluten-free beignet  or the  no sugar added you get people with  requests all the time for the  gluten-free and can you sell sandwiches  and can you do this and can you do that  why i mean when you do something well  when you continue to do it and and  people seem to enjoy it you know we just  stick with what you do best i think cafe  dumont does that 24 7 364. with the  original location only scheduled to be  closed christmas day and while the doors  have been shut by hurricanes like  katrina and more recently with the  pandemic roman says opening them back up  is also a part of that family tradition  looking at this and having  all these people enjoy them some for the  first time does that ever get old no  never gets old makes it worth getting up  every morning to see everything all the  happy faces of some of the young  children eating their first beignet it  makes it all worthwhile  [Music]  first or 50th i don't know which one i'm  on you guys have your beignets i have  mine i did ask how much powdered sugar  they go through in a week and he said a  couple tons a couple tons but wow so  good they are so good  the only thing that's changed in all  those years dana is the price i remember  when a beignet or three beignets were a  buck and a cup of coffee was a buck and  now i'm i'm sure it's well over that  this coffee is done you know what i  don't remember actually  but they're delicious they're so good i  don't think they're actually that  expensive michelle honestly it's like  two or three bucks now but you know i  always and the lines are outrageous now  i'm sorry about it right but worth it so  worth it  so good okay  thank you

